    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who claims the top spot in our lineup. His favorable matchup against Feltner (xERA 4.69) combined with a leadoff slot and a massive 17% boost for SP skill creates an ideal environment for his speed to impact the SB category. He is joined in the elite tier by **Christian Yelich** (74.67) and **Kyle Schwarber** (69.09). **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from the leadoff spot and a 13% platoon edge against Cecconi, while **Kyle Schwarber** continues to be a core engine for our HR and RBI production, boasting an elite 0.388 xwOBA that keeps him as a set-and-forget option despite neutral platoon variance.\n\nStrategic optimization favored high-efficiency matchups today, forcing **Lars Nootbaar** (54.90) to the bench. While his 11% platoon edge against King was promising, he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace starters like **Luke Raley** or **Junior Caminero**. **Junior Caminero** (61.08) remains a high-leverage start, as his third-spot lineup projection provides essential stability even against the left-handed Wrobleski. We are keeping a close watch on **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Christian Yelich**, **Luke Raley**, **Carson Benge**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** regarding their official lineup placement; should any of these players drop lower in their respective orders, their efficiency scores will tighten, potentially narrowing the gap between them and reserves like **Caleb Durbin** or **Colt Keith**. We are effectively mitigating risk by benching **Caleb Durbin** and **Colt Keith** against elite-tier arms like Cease and Brown, prioritizing the favorable strike zones offered by the projected matchups for our active lineup.",
